    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48994" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trībŭlo</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>,
				ātum, 1, v. a.
			tribulum. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>to press</i>:
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θλίβω</span> tribulo, presso, premo.
			Gloss, Philox.; Cato. R. R.  23,
			4.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to oppress</i>, <i>afflict</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in omnibus tribulemur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Gnost. 13 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ambros. Serm. 22</span></i>, n. 1;
					<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Hist. Eccl. 1,
		11</span></i>.</div>
